Role description and responsibilities
Damia is a specialist tech recruitment agency in Portugal, focused on technology, product, and engineering roles. We work with funded scaleups, international companies building teams in Portugal, and established tech organisations scaling critical hires. 
Our approach is consultative, not transactional. Every mandate runs through a structured methodology, from strategic discovery and talent mapping to curated shortlists and post-hire follow-up, led by senior recruiters who understand the market and the roles they recruit for. 
We are part of the Triveris Group ecosystem alongside We Are META and Landing.Jobs, giving us reach across the full spectrum of tech talent in Portugal. 

Damia supports its clients with direct hires.

Who are they looking for?
Being a Senior Consultant comes with an exciting & challenging role. Their senior consultants work on billable engagements to design, develop and implement solutions by using standard or new methods, techniques and top IT Tech solutions, consistently delivering high client value.

This senior consultant will work on our Data and Artificial Intelligence team, analyzing, creating and implementing new technical and business solutions, developing pre-sales and project management activities as well as mentoring team members.

This role will be part of a technology consultancy team with vast mission-critical application experience, working with major clients in different sectors.

What is the challenge?
In this role, you will:

• Design and lead end-to-end AI architectures in collaboration with business and technical teams;
• Translate business requirements into scalable, secure and resilient technical solutions;
• Define and integrate AI systems across data, infrastructure and application layers;
• Ensure compliance with security, privacy and resilience-by-design principles;
• Stay aligned with emerging AI and GenAI trends and technologies;
• Participate in large-scale client engagements;
• Ability to identify fundamental problems from real-world cloud use-cases and design, build, and validate successful AI solutions;
• Solution architecture and design experience, translating business requirements into technical specifications, and developing scalable and robust AI solutions;
• Strategic mindset combined with execution strength, able to structure complex challenges into actionable roadmaps;

Requirements
Technical skills

• +2 years in Technical Architecture roles, with AI exposure;
• Bachelor's degree or MS degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Informatics, Data Science;
• Microsoft Certification: Azure AI Engineer or Azure Data Scientist Associate is a plus;
• Experience building AI products using LLMs, embeddings or other natural language technologies, particularly leveraging Vector Search;
• Experience with RAG, embeddings, vector databases and semantic search;
• Knowledge of LLM integration, prompt engineering, guardrails and AI observability;
• Understanding of AI governance, security and responsible AI principles;
• Experience integrating enterprise AI services (Azure Foundry);
• Knowledge of secure architecture (identity, access, secrets management).

Soft & other skills

• Commitment to continuous learning and staying updated with advancements in the field of AI;
• Excellent Communication Skills;
• Customer-focused;
• Consultative profile with good organisational and documentation skills
• Experience in leading customer meetings and other customer interactions.

At Flix, we offer a dynamic work environment with competitive pay, strong growth opportunities, and a tech-driven approach to making travel more accessible, sustainable, and affordable. &nbsp;

As a&nbsp; Jr. Accounts Payable Accountant (m/f/d) , you will be a part of the Central Accounting team . You will be responsible for processing invoices, managing vendor payments, reconciling accounts, and ensuring accurate financial records.

This role is based in Sofia, Bulgaria (hybrid model).

About the Role

• Process on timely basis&nbsp;accounts&nbsp;payable transactions&nbsp;

• Monitor vendor open items and clarifies old and unusual balances&nbsp;

• Prepares accounts payable reconciliations and clarify differences&nbsp;

• Prepares and executes electronic payment runs as well as manual payments if necessary&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Assists in the collection and distribution of financial information&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Prepare clear and concise documentation&nbsp;on working procedures&nbsp;

About You

• Bachelor’s degree in accounting&nbsp;or equivalent&nbsp;

• 1-3 years of experience in&nbsp;Accounting&nbsp;

• Solid knowledge in Accounting, VAT knowledge -would be an advantage, but not mandatory

• Ability to thrive in a fast-growing international environment&nbsp;

• Confident handling of MS Office&nbsp;

• Reliability and organizational skills&nbsp;

• Fluent in English language&nbsp;

We recognize that everyone carries a unique set of valuable skills and experiences. If you think you could have an impact even though you don't meet 100% of the requirements, we still encourage you to apply. We want to hear from you! &nbsp;

What We Offer

• Travel perks : 12 free Flix vouchers + 12 discount vouchers for friends &amp; family.&nbsp;

• Hybrid work model : We are an office-first company, but we offer flexibility to balance work and life.&nbsp;

• Wellbeing support : Access confidential 1:1 counselling, courses, and stress management for yourself and up to four family members.&nbsp;

• Learning &amp; Development : Take advantage of language classes, training courses, and expert-led sessions to grow your skills.&nbsp;

• Mentoring Program : Connect with experienced colleagues to gain insights and accelerate your career.&nbsp;

